<div class="hero">
  <h1>Registered Dietitian Nutritionists in Cary, NC</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Stepping Stones Nutrition is a team of Registered Dietitian Nutritionists in Cary, NC, specializing in eating disorders, pediatric nutrition, and intuitive eating, all through a weight-inclusive lens. We provide compassionate, evidence-based nutrition therapy for children, teens, and adults.</p>
</div>

<div class="team-member">
  <img src="/images/team/bryn-boyer.png" alt="Bryn Boyer, RDN, LDN">
  <div class="bio">
    <h4>Bryn Boyer, RDN, LDN &mdash; Owner &amp; Registered Dietitian Nutritionist</h4>
    <p>Bryn is a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN), and a Licensed Dietitian/Nutritionist (LDN). She has been working in the field of disordered eating for over 18 years. She worked in the Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP) for the Eating Disorder Treatment Center (EDTC) in Bucks, PA. She started her work in private practice nutrition therapy at Body Honor Nutrition and Wellness in Moorestown, NJ. Bryn opened her first private practice, Boyer Nutrition, in Media, PA, and West Chester, PA. She has been practicing nutrition therapy for disordered eating in Cary and Raleigh since 2015.</p>
    <p>Bryn attended Virginia Tech where she received her Bachelor of Science Degree in Human Nutrition, Food and Exercise, with a double concentration in Dietetics; and Science of Food, Nutrition and Exercise. She completed her dietetic internship at the University of California San Francisco. She started her dietetic career in Northern Virginia (where she was born and raised) as a dietitian and personal trainer.</p>
    <p>Bryn enjoys working with all populations&hellip;children, teens, college students, student athletes, and adults at all stages of life.</p>
    <p>Bryn is a member of the International Association of Eating Disorder Professionals and the International Federation of Eating Disorder Dietitians.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="team-member">
  <img src="/images/team/summer-daley.png" alt="Summer Daley, RDN, LDN">
  <div class="bio">
    <h4>Summer Daley, RDN, LDN &mdash; Registered Dietitian Nutritionist</h4>
    <p>Summer is a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN), and a Licensed Dietitian/Nutritionist (LDN). Summer has experience working with eating disorder clients of all ages and populations. She has a passion for helping others reconnect with food, exploring the positive benefits, functions, and healing food brings to the body, and allowing oneself to nourish themselves again without shame, guilt, or fear.</p>
    <p>Summer has eating disorder experience at the residential, partial hospitalization (PHP), and intensive outpatient (IOP) levels of care at an eating disorder treatment center in Durham, North Carolina. Summer received her Bachelor of Science (BS) degree in Nutrition and Dietetics from Appalachian State University. During her dietetic internship, she worked at the North Carolina Specialty Hospital, the Interfaith Food Shuttle, North Carolina State University, and The Cypress of Raleigh.</p>
    <p>In her free time, Summer enjoys baking, hiking, exploring different coffee shops around the area and spending time with her husband and friends. Summer is excited to help support and guide you in your journey of finding joy, strength, and healing in your relationship with food again!</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="block">
  <h4>Locations We Serve</h4>
  <p><strong>North Carolina</strong> &mdash; We are local to Cary and offer in-person and telehealth appts to clients and families in Cary, Apex, Morrisville, Raleigh, Fuquay-Varina, Garner, Holly Springs, and other surrounding areas. We offer telehealth appts. to clients and families throughout all of North Carolina.</p>
  <p><strong>Beyond North Carolina</strong> &mdash; We support clients and families via telehealth in Arizona, California, Colorado, Michigan, and Virginia. We offer in-person and telehealth appointments.</p>
</section>

